 "integration": {
  "summary": "Write NetworkCtrl to run or stop the unit, set summer/winter with SuWiNetworkChgover after setting SuWiChgSrc to BMS, and adjust the fan, economy, humidity and air-quality setpoints as needed. Read the operating mode and status, supply and controlled temperatures and the general alarm.",
  "minimum_points": [
   {
    "ref": "MV 24562",
    "name": "NetworkCtrl",
    "why": "Network on/off (1 = Off, 2 = On)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "MV 28594",
    "name": "SuWiNetworkChgover",
    "why": "Summer/winter command (1 = Winter, 2 = Summer)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "MV 9493",
    "name": "SuWiChgSrc",
    "why": "Must be 3 = BMS for the summer/winter command"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 52572",
    "name": "SplyFanSpvSt1Spv",
    "why": "Supply fan setpoint (units per SplyEngUnit)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "MV 39130",
    "name": "AckAlmPls",
    "why": "Acknowledge all alarms (2 = On)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "MV 6080",
    "name": "ActOpMode",
    "why": "Operating mode (Off/On/Ventilation/Economy/Standby)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "MV 32321",
    "name": "ActOpSta",
    "why": "Why the unit runs or stops (e.g. 11 = BMS)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 45150",
    "name": "SupplyTmp",
    "why": "Supply air temperature"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 52988",
    "name": "ActCtrlVal",
    "why": "Temperature being controlled"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BO 5714",
    "name": "AlmOutHigh",
    "why": "General alarm (1 = Alarm)"
   }
  ],
  "enable": "NetworkCtrl (MV 24562, \"Network source\", 1 = Off / 2 = On) is the writable on/off object; ActOpSta (MV 32321) reports 11 = BMS when the network is in control. Summer/winter changeover follows the BMS only when SuWiChgSrc (MV 9493) = 3 (BMS); then write SuWiNetworkChgover (MV 28594). The guide gives no further procedure.",
  "heartbeat": null,
  "remote_sensors": null,
  "setup": [
   "BACnet IP comes from a POL908 module and BACnet MS/TP from a POL904 module plugged onto the MicroTech controller.",
   "BACnet IP defaults: device instance 1, UDP port 47808, DHCP off; set Apply Changes = Yes after editing, which restarts the controller.",
   "BACnet MS/TP module defaults: MAC address 24, 38400 baud, Max Master 127, Max Info Frames 1; the device instance is derived from the production number and date code. Cycle power after changing the address.",
